      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "General protocol for 1–3: to a stirred solution of LH3 in methanol (30 mL) was added Ln(NO3)3·xH2O (x = 5 for 1). Tetra-n-butylammonium hydroxide (TBAH, 25% in MeOH) was added dropwise and the mixture was stirred for 15 min, then pivalic acid (PivH) was added. The mixture was heated under reflux for 6 h, giving a clear yellow solution, cooled to room temperature, filtered, and the filtrate evaporated in vacuum. The residue was washed with diethyl ether, dried, dissolved in chloroform/acetonitrile (3:1), and crystallized by slow evaporation at room temperature for 7–10 days. For 1: LH3 (0.072 g, 0.23 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.104 g, 0.23 mmol), TBAH (0.62 mL, 0.57 mmol), PivH (0.036 g, 0.34 mmol).",
